# Setup incomplete: staged setup tasks

This file was written by the setup wizard on {{DATE}}. It is the to-do list
for the AI assistant's setup sessions in this project. Setup is staged over
more than one session, with asynchronous work between sessions, so no single
sitting drags. Work the tasks in order, mark each one done here as it
completes, and delete this file only when every task is done.

Tasks marked (with user) need {{USER_NAME}} present. Tasks marked (async) do
not: run them between sessions, in parallel subagents where that helps, and
mark their outputs "draft, awaiting review" until {{USER_NAME}} has confirmed
them in the next session.

## Tasks

### Session A: intake (with user)

1. Run the intake interview in `core/intake.md` and record the answers there.
2. Build `core/profile.md`, including a fit bar appropriate to someone who is
   {{EMPLOYMENT_STATUS}}: what a new role must offer before it is worth moving for.
3. Ask {{USER_NAME}} to drop their existing CV (any format) into
   `core/source/`, and confirm the target directions the field research
   should cover (intake question 2).

### Between sessions (async)

4. Synthesise a draft `core/master-cv.md` from the source CV. Always produce
   two outputs: the best draft the material supports, and a gap list of what
   the source could not tell you (roles without outcomes, missing dates, thin
   evidence, unexplained periods). Never pad gaps with invention.
5. Research {{USER_NAME}}'s target field and draft `core/industry-brief.md`:
   how hiring works there, what recruiters prioritise, CV and letter
   conventions, market state. Follow the guidance at the top of that file.
6. Confirm the tracker works: read and write `tracker/applications.csv` as
   described in `tracker/tracker.md`.

   Tasks 4 and 5 are independent, so they suit parallel subagents; review
   any subagent output for accuracy before it reaches {{USER_NAME}}.

### Session B: review (with user)

7. Walk {{USER_NAME}} through the master CV draft. Where the gap list is
   substantial, run a CV interview driven by it, filling the gaps from what
   {{USER_NAME}} actually did.
8. Present the industry brief for review; it steers nothing until
   {{USER_NAME}} corrects and confirms it.
9. Seed `core/stories.md` and `core/voice.md`, harvesting the CV interview
   and the conversation so far.

### Session C: finishing (with user)

10. Set up the render templates: help {{USER_NAME}} choose a Typst Universe
    CV template (https://typst.app/universe), or replicate their existing CV
    design from an example they provide, and vendor it into
    `render/templates/` so `main.typ` and `cover-letter.typ` exist and
    `render.sh` works end to end; verify with a real render of a dummy slug.
11. Delete this file and tell {{USER_NAME}} the project is ready to judge
    fits and draft applications.

